# SkausWatch - Security Infrastructure Application
## Implementation Plan & Todo List

### Project Overview
A comprehensive security infrastructure platform using Python 3.13, py4web, and pyDAL with async/threading optimizations.
Four containerized services: Manager, PKI Server, SSH CA Server, and AAA Log Analyzer.

---

## Phase 1: Foundation & Architecture

### 1.1 Project Structure Setup
- [ ] Initialize project with Python 3.13 requirements
- [ ] Set up pyproject.toml with modern Python packaging
- [ ] Configure pre-commit hooks for code quality
- [ ] Establish monorepo structure with service subdirectories
  ```
  SkausWatch/
  ├── website/           # Marketing website (Node.js/Next.js)
  ├── docs/              # Comprehensive documentation
  ├── services/
  │   ├── manager/
  │   ├── pki/
  │   ├── sshca/
  │   └── monitor/
  ├── shared/
  │   ├── models/
  │   ├── utils/
  │   └── security/
  └── deployment/
  ```

### 1.2 Base Dependencies & Configuration
- [ ] Create requirements.txt for each service
  - py4web (latest)
  - pyDAL (latest)
  - cryptography
  - asyncio
  - aiohttp
  - celery for task queue
  - redis for caching/sessions
  - prometheus-client for metrics
- [ ] Set up logging infrastructure with structured logging
- [ ] Configure environment variable management (python-dotenv)

### 1.3 Container Configuration
- [ ] Create Dockerfile for each service with multi-stage builds
- [ ] Implement docker-compose.yml for local development
- [ ] Configure Kubernetes manifests for production
- [ ] Set up health check endpoints for each service
- [ ] Implement graceful shutdown handlers

